  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Community Structures for Preparedness and Response (E-CSPaR) in Zambia</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Empowering Community Structures for Preparedness and Response (E-CSPaR) is a  preparedness initiative implemented by the British Red Cross through IFRC, with technical support from UKHSA and coordination from ZNPHI, to strengthen Zambia&#x2019;s district and community-level capacity to prevent, detect and respond to outbreaks, particularly cholera, while complementing the Nutrition Programme&#x2019;s efforts to address the links between malnutrition and disease. The project supports the Government of Zambia to operationalise the CATI approach by establishing fully equipped CATI coordination cells and response teams; integrating CATI responsibilities into district health personnel job descriptions; maintaining comprehensive and deployable CATI kits; embedding CATI oversight and ringfenced financing within District Incident Management Systems; adapting national cholera guidance into district-level SOPs; conducting annual simulation exercises; putting in place strong record-keeping systems; ensuring after-action reviews for all outbreak responses; and enabling government and partner community health workers to conduct enhanced community-based surveillance and risk-reduction activities for cholera and other public-health threats such as Mpox, Marburg and Anthrax.</narrative>
  </description>
